# Local build: use venv

For local QMK builds in this repo, use the project’s Python virtual environment at `.venv`. Do not assume or recommend a system-wide `qmk` install.

## Running builds

- **Preferred**: Activate the venv, then run `qmk` or `make`:
  ```bash
  source .venv/bin/activate
  qmk compile -kb <keyboard> -km <keymap> [options]
  ```
- **Without activating**: Call the venv’s `qmk` explicitly (from repo root):
  ```bash
  .venv/bin/qmk compile -kb <keyboard> -km <keymap> [options]
  ```
- **With make** (e.g. `make git-submodule`): Either activate first, or set:
  ```bash
  make <target> QMK_BIN="$(pwd)/.venv/bin/qmk"
  ```

## One-time setup

If `.venv` is missing or broken, see `docs/local_build_venv.md` for full setup (venv creation, `pip install -r requirements.txt`, `pip install qmk`, `qmk setup`, submodules).

## When suggesting commands

When suggesting compile, flash, or other QMK CLI commands in this project, use one of the patterns above so the venv is used.
